<!-- ── Listen-friendly content ────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display:none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: Zone of Proximal Policy Optimization</h2>
    <p>ZPPO solves a fundamental problem in small-model RL training. When a 0.8B student fails every rollout on a hard question, GRPO's group-relative advantage collapses to zero — the student gets no gradient signal on exactly the questions it needs most. Knowledge distillation appears to help but silently hurts: imitating a larger teacher's logits concentrates the student on the teacher's paths, degrading generalization on any benchmark beyond the training corpus.</p>
    <p>ZPPO's answer is to keep the teacher inside the prompt, never inside the gradient. For hard questions, BCQ places one correct teacher response and one wrong student response as anonymous candidates the student must discriminate. NCQ aggregates all the student's wrong rollouts into a single prompt, showing their shared failure patterns. A prompt replay buffer re-exposes each hard question with fresh candidates until the student masters it. The gains are largest at 0.8B (+9.3 pp on VLM benchmarks, +7.9 pp on LLM benchmarks) and decrease with model size — the pattern of a method that works precisely where the zone of proximal development is widest.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：近侧发展区策略优化</h2>
    <p>ZPPO解决了小模型强化学习训练中的一个根本问题。当0.8B的学生模型在某道难题上所有推理均失败时，GRPO的组相对优势会归零——学生恰恰在最需要帮助的题目上得不到任何梯度信号。知识蒸馏表面上有所帮助，实则悄悄有害：模仿更大教师模型的logit分布，会让学生集中于教师已走过的路径，导致在训练语料库之外的基准测试中泛化能力下降。</p>
    <p>ZPPO的解决方案是将教师知识放入提示中，而非放入梯度中。对于难题，BCQ将一个教师的正确回答和一个学生的错误回答作为匿名候选项并排呈现，让学生通过推理加以辨别；NCQ将学生所有错误的推理过程聚合到同一个提示中，暴露其共有的错误模式；提示重放缓冲区在每次访问时以新的候选项重新呈现每道难题，直到学生掌握为止。增益在0.8B模型上最为显著（VLM基准+9.3个百分点，LLM基准+7.9个百分点），并随模型规模增大而递减——这正是一种在近侧发展区最宽时效果最强的方法的规律。</p>
  </div>
</div>

